TARRANT COUNTY RESULTS ARE “TROUBLING TO SAY THE LEAST” FOR PAXTON

@stinchfield1776 says the early numbers out of Tarrant County are a major warning sign for Ken Paxton, with James Talarico leading there by roughly 20 points and about 80% of the vote reported.

“The numbers do not look good.”

Stinchfield notes Tarrant has long been considered one of the strongest Republican counties in the country and says Denton County is showing a similarly concerning pattern.

@DallasXCEO, reporting from Tarrant County, was even more blunt: “It’s a bloodbath for Republicans.”

Both cautioned that Election Day votes could still change the picture, but said the margins in two traditionally red counties are far from what Republicans wanted to see.
